# What `git archive` -- and so the GitHub release zipball, which a
# Zenodo deposit takes -- leaves out: the lab (lab/, the dnsjax-lab
# package of flows and features in development), every file written
# for coding agents (the CLAUDE.md notes, .claude/), the development
# configuration (CI, git and hook settings, uv's pinned interpreter and
# lock file), and the contributor guide, which describes this
# repository rather than the solver.  The PyPI sdist holds the same files
# (pyproject.toml's source-include): change the two together.
/lab export-ignore
/CONTRIBUTING.md export-ignore
/uv.lock export-ignore
/.claude export-ignore
CLAUDE.md export-ignore
/.github export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
/.gitignore export-ignore
/.python-version export-ignore
/prek.toml export-ignore
